#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "520b96bb-95ea-55e5-ae87-1b02165294f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371745} {:answer/id #uuid "f04b7563-6361-5bd9-a431-f4e78ee12a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371746} {:answer/id #uuid "879e1ffb-632a-5095-8792-8453fa0fb890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371747} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4e5260-7e39-5028-b15f-5686d56067bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371748} {:answer/id #uuid "3c783b67-8495-54fb-bbfb-eed70a4350e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "879e1ffb-632a-5095-8792-8453fa0fb890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371747} :answer-field/id #uuid "6323f818-ad86-5871-8ae3-ad2699161d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16ee071c-dc61-52a6-97dd-99854448ee3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132003" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcfeeb69-27e6-5b5b-9004-0e05bb260a4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "234" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371752} {:answer/id #uuid "5f89018a-ae0c-57a5-a5a3-8cbfd22b5e62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371753} {:answer/id #uuid "c54b94c8-1002-5bb0-9b71-401fe64a4815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371754} {:answer/id #uuid "01b8cd19-f7ee-588b-a719-a58acc0a1ece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "304" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371755} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed58fb5-1434-5b8f-a88f-2e72116c7121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "312" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f89018a-ae0c-57a5-a5a3-8cbfd22b5e62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "340" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371753} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c377356-42c5-57be-bfb7-316cb0a18d54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cc5bbef-3b38-57a9-8cd0-0b1ff80a0540" :question/math-academy-id "q-132146" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10(25+9) \\\\  & =340.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "add1c357-3a7d-5e86-b8ea-f4edf8ad51d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118636} {:answer/id #uuid "cf77a243-53af-5d0f-855a-b9871af105ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "124" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118637} {:answer/id #uuid "303570f5-20c1-5aea-a5c4-622fce3228fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-504" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118638} {:answer/id #uuid "544fbade-bad4-59e5-bdfb-b11cac073d8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118639} {:answer/id #uuid "64ef0566-ac1a-59dd-88dd-570a8761323a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64ef0566-ac1a-59dd-88dd-570a8761323a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118640} :answer-field/id #uuid "9100f6ae-6260-577d-8a46-50b7c53ad890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37774ae0-a0cd-5a39-9730-2063497da256" :question/math-academy-id "q-42559" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-2){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-28+40) \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf520dcf-d62d-5fee-8732-82095c413c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371758} {:answer/id #uuid "69d529a8-4976-5f9d-96d2-840474a2a7a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371759} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec8b9b6-3a0e-54d7-8944-b8b09376e640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371760} {:answer/id #uuid "59854289-3c73-57b6-99c8-2d80827b4db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371761} {:answer/id #uuid "8d4c701c-cfdd-592f-9105-290d859732ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59854289-3c73-57b6-99c8-2d80827b4db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371761} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17bb7ab-7a60-595c-ace6-137ebe5a3991" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a2b160-a569-5696-8596-179bbcebb9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-91220" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307043d0-7464-5cf2-97b9-c8c906f9a039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371765} {:answer/id #uuid "68c53f8d-7bc3-5fd5-93a0-94c653f71247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371766} {:answer/id #uuid "bba49d8c-6671-5cc4-b6f3-6419f01356b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371767} {:answer/id #uuid "ca979a87-40a5-507b-a8f2-549f278b2145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371768} {:answer/id #uuid "d3182fd5-446d-59dd-86db-cfa2612690b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c53f8d-7bc3-5fd5-93a0-94c653f71247" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371766} :answer-field/id #uuid "5392364c-2ade-5143-acf9-62d56cad907e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c634aee-e652-57bc-9f32-1580a82e9134" :question/math-academy-id "q-91221" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-4){C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
